# Parameters vs Arguments

- **Parameters** are the variables listed in the method definition.
- **Arguments** are the actual values you pass when calling the method.

```csharp
// 'speed' is a parameter
void Move(float speed)
{
    transform.Translate(speed * Time.deltaTime, 0, 0);
}

// 5f is an argument
Move(5f);
```

Parameters allow the method to work with different data each time.

# Passing More Data

You can define any number of parameters, separated by commas:

```csharp
void SetPlayerInfo(string name, int health, float speed)
{
    Debug.Log($"{name} | HP: {health} | Speed: {speed}");
}
```

Call it:
```csharp
SetPlayerInfo("Luigi", 120, 8.5f);
```

Order matters! Arguments must match the parameter order.

